.TH GPUTEST 1
.SH NAME
gputest \- render and check a VirGL triangle
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gputest
[
.B -t
]
[
.B -o
.I image
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Gputest
uses
.IR gpu (3)
to render a coloured triangle in a 400 by 300 pixel off-screen image.
It checks the background colour, interpolated centre colour, and triangle
area after reading the image back from the GPU.
It then displays the result in a window; type
.B q
or delete to exit.
.PP
The
.B -t
option performs the rendering checks without opening a window.
The
.B -o
option writes the result in Plan 9 image format to
.I image
and exits without opening a window.
Both work from the serial console.
.PP
The program uses native Plan 9 C and libraries.
It sends VirGL commands and TGSI shader text to the host renderer;
it does not provide an OpenGL API.
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/cmd/gputest
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR gpu (3),
.IR image (6)
